    <string name="action_save">Сохранить</string>
    <!--
      «Готово» closes a picker; «Сохранить» writes. All three modals — date, time, duration — used to
      confirm with «Сохранить», so booking a lesson asked the tutor to save twice in a row and the
      first one plausibly read as having committed the booking. Picking a date saves nothing.
    -->
    <string name="action_done">Готово</string>
    <string name="action_cancel">Отмена</string>
    <string name="action_ok">Понятно</string>
    <string name="action_back">Назад</string>
    <string name="action_archive">В архив</string>
    <string name="action_unarchive">Из архива</string>
    <string name="action_enable">Включить</string>
    <!--
      Undo is «Вернуть», not «Отменить» — this is an app where «Отменено» is a *lesson status*. On the
      snackbar that follows deleting a payment, «Отменить» read as "cancel something" at least as
      readily as "put the payment back", which is the one thing the button does. «Отмена» stays on
      dialogs, where dismissing is all it can mean.
    -->
    <string name="action_undo">Вернуть</string>
    <!-- The action a snackbar carries when the message names something to go and look at. -->
    <string name="action_show">Показать</string>
    <string name="action_more">Ещё действия</string>

    <!--
      What a field says when it is wrong, and when it is merely required.

      A form gates its «Сохранить» on `canSave` and used to say nothing else, so a tutor looking at a
      disabled button had to work out which of six boxes was the problem. The money fields were worse than
      silent: they drew a red outline with no message at all — fixed everywhere, since the classification
      is `MoneyField.error`'s and every money input goes through it. `field_required` is only on the group
      form so far; the student and booking forms still name no required field.
    -->
    <string name="field_required">Обязательное поле</string>
    <!--
      Short on purpose: it shows in the supporting line of every money field in the app, and an example
      says more than «Неверная сумма» in the same room. (It was written for the student form's per-subject
      price box while that was 140dp wide beside a checkbox; the box is full-width and stacked now, so the
      constraint has gone — the wording is kept because it is better, not because it has to be.)
    -->
    <string name="money_error_unreadable">Например: 25 или 25,50</string>
    <string name="money_error_zero_payment">Платёж не может быть нулевым</string>

